<title>JAPAN: Japan Energy to shut 90,200 bpd topper from Apr 10.</title>
<headline>Japan Energy to shut 90,200 bpd topper from Apr 10.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Energy Corp said on Friday it plans to close a 90,200 barrels-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit at its Mizushima plant in western Japan for rountine maintenance checks from April 10.</p>
<p>The topper will resume operations late May, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The other topper at the plant, which has a crude processing capacity of 110,000 bpd, will continue operating as normal for the remainder of the year.</p>
</text>
